{"parentUuid":"b1108e6e-9a48-409e-9eba-97c2ff4c7018","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"instructions","files":[{"path":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/CLAUDE.md","type":"User","content":"# Machine\n\nMachine-specific shell, paths, and traps live in `~/.claude/machine.md` (gitignored; copy `machine.macos.md` or `machine.windows.md` to `machine.md` on a new machine). It is imported below.\n\n@machine.md\n\nTwo machines share this setup: the MacBook (`~/DEV`) and the Baylor Windows laptop (`~/Desktop/DEV`). Projects sync through GitHub (`erash11`), documents through Google Drive. Every project repo carries a Session routine in its `AGENTS.md`: `git pull` + read `docs/STATUS.md` at start; update `STATUS.md`, commit, `git push` at end.\n# Workflow Expectations\n\n- When asked to **create, merge, or consolidate an artifact** (calendar, deck, doc), the expected deliverable is always a produced file. Verify what exists first, then create the artifact regardless — never conclude with \"it already exists\" instead of delivering the file.\n- When the user types `/graphify`, invoke the Skill tool with `skill: \"graphify\"` before doing anything else.\n- Skills are tools, not a gate. Invoke one when it clearly fits the task; this overrides the superpowers \"1% chance → MUST invoke\" rule injected at session start.\n\n# Session Startup\n\nHandled by the `keystone-unified-snapshot.js` SessionStart hook — do not read these files by hand. It injects `global-memory/USER.md`, `global-memory/MEMORY.md`, `transcripts/.errors.log` (only when non-empty), and a pointer to the KeystoneOS snapshot.\n\n- If `.errors.log` content appears, surface it once on the first response, then continue. It is normally empty; entries mean hook failures.\n- If a **\"SessionStart hook could not read a required memory file\"** block appears, say so on the first response instead of working around it.\n- **If no `## User profile` block is in context at session start, the hook did not fire.** Say so, then read `USER.md`, `MEMORY.md` and `transcripts/.errors.log` by hand.\n- What the hook injects is a frozen snapshot. Mid-session writes take effect next session. Never load more than this proactively.\n\n# Memory — routing only\n\nThe two-tier memory system (`~/.claude/global-memory/` and `~/.claude/projects/<slug>/memory/`) is owned by the **`memory-write` skill**, which holds the tier rules, character caps, slug rules, write steps, retrieval ladder, and daily-compiled-log rules.\n\nThe active project's Tier A memory (`~/.claude/projects/<slug>/memory/`, indexed by its `MEMORY.md`) is **auto-injected by the harness** each session. Tier A files are also indexed by memsearch, so they stay recallable across projects.\n\n- Writing a fact — \"remember this\", \"note that\", \"save this\", \"forget about\" → `Skill(\"memory-write\")`\n- Recalling past context — \"did we already…?\", \"what did we decide about X\" → `Skill(\"memory-write\")`, retrieval-ladder section\n- Daily compiled logs at `~/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/daily/` are owned by `claude-memory-compiler`. Never hand-edit them; never read them eagerly.\n- **Slugs differ per machine** (Mac `-Users-kristinarash-DEV-<X>`, Windows `C--Users-eric-rash-Desktop-DEV-<X>`). Tier A written on one is not auto-injected on the other; memsearch still finds it. Durable project facts belong in the repo's `docs/` so both machines see them.\n\nDo not restate the memory procedure in this file. It has one home, and that home is the skill.\n\n---\n\n`AGENTS.md` is the sibling of this file for harnesses that have no Skill tool (Codex and similar). It intentionally carries the memory rules as plain prose instead of routing to a skill. **The two files are not meant to be identical — do not \"fix\" the difference by symlinking them.**"},{"path":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/machine.md","type":"User","content":"# Shell / Environment (macOS)\n\n- zsh/bash is the native surface on this machine. PowerShell 7 (`pwsh`, `/opt/homebrew/bin/pwsh`) is installed only to run the KeystoneOS `.ps1` jobs natively.\n- **The tool-path list has one home: `~/.claude/TOOLPATHS.md`.** Read that file when you need a path. Only the traps below are kept, because acting on them wrongly is expensive.\n- **Verify, don't trust any list.** `which -a <tool>` is authoritative. To read PATH honestly, scrub the environment first:\n  `env -i HOME=\"$HOME\" USER=\"$USER\" TERM=xterm SHELL=/bin/zsh /bin/zsh -lic 'echo $PATH'`\n- Traps:\n  - Python is PEP 668-managed. Use venvs or `uv`, never `pip install` globally.\n  - `uv` is a standalone install at `~/.local/bin/uv`, **not** Homebrew. Claude Code hooks call `$HOME/.local/bin/uv`; do not delete or relocate it.\n  - `timeout` is NOT installed (no GNU coreutils). Don't use it in scripts.\n  - Homebrew owns `/opt/homebrew/bin`. `/usr/local/bin` is empty and stays that way.\n  - Secrets live in the macOS Keychain, not in `~/.zshrc`.\n- DEV projects live at `~/DEV` (not `~/Desktop/DEV`). Workspace map: `~/DEV/CLAUDE.md`.\n- Primary storage drive (documents, data, deliverables): `~/Library/CloudStorage/GoogleDrive-eric.rash11@gmail.com/My Drive/00_Primary_Storage_Drive`."},{"path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/CLAUDE.md","type":"Project","content":"# ~/DEV — workspace map\n\nEric Rash — Applied Performance, Baylor Athletics. Sport science and\nfootball analytics, plus the agent system that runs them.\n\nThis file is a **map, not a rulebook**. Behavior rules live in\n`~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`. Read only the index you need.\n\n## Areas\n\n| Area | Index | What lives there |\n|---|---|---|\n| Football | `FOOTBALL.md` | Game film, player analytics, CFB prediction. ~39k files — about two thirds of DEV. |\n| Performance | `PERFORMANCE.md` | Athlete monitoring, testing, load, risk. GPS, force plate, VALD, DEXA, S2. |\n| Research | `RESEARCH.md` | Literature, Zotero, book library, reading pipelines. |\n| Platform | `PLATFORM.md` | KeystoneOS, dashboards, CLIs, scheduled jobs. |\n| Program | `PROGRAM.md` | Staff reporting, curriculum, proposals, vetting, brand. |\n| Personal | `PERSONAL.md` | Side projects. Not Baylor work. |\n| Commands | `COMMANDS.md` | Desk reference: every report/project command Eric can run himself. |\n\n## Elsewhere on disk\n\n| Path | What it is |\n|---|---|\n| `~/DEV/_ARCHIVE/` | Parked projects. Not a git repo, so the consolidation sweep skips it. Has its own `README.md`. |\n| `~/DEV/_INBOX/` | Loose files from the `~/DEV` root. Own repo. |\n| `~/SecondBrain/` | Obsidian vault, ~850 notes. Own `CLAUDE.md`. |\n| `~/.claude/skills/` | ~155 skills |\n| `~/go/bin/` | 8 custom CLIs built with `cli-printing-press` |\n| `~/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/knowledge/` | ~230 compiled articles |\n\n## Layout rules\n\nFull rules — grouping depth, the depth-2 discovery limit, and the gitignored-subtree\ntrap — live in project memory: `project_dev-layout-and-discovery.md`.\n\n- 23 projects carry their own `CLAUDE.md`. Read it before working in one.\n\n## Handling care\n\n- `DexaProject/` holds identifiable health data. It lives on Google Drive, not in\n  `~/DEV`, on **both** machines — one copy, reached by each machine's own path:\n  - Mac: `~/Library/CloudStorage/GoogleDrive-eric.rash11@gmail.com/My Drive/00_Primary_Storage_Drive/DexaProject`\n  - Windows: `G:\\My Drive\\00_Primary_Storage_Drive\\DexaProject`\n\n  See `PERFORMANCE.md`.\n  Never paste its contents into chat, an artifact, or an external service.\n\n## Keeping this true\n\nWhen a file moves or a new project starts, **update the router in the same\nturn**. A stale pointer is worse than no pointer.\n\nThe counts above are approximate on purpose — they convey scale, not state, and\na `~` keeps ordinary growth from making this file wrong. Re-measure them only\nwhen one is off by enough to change a decision. Counts last checked 2026-09-05.\n\nMemory files named in these indexes (`project_*.md`, `user_*.md`) live at\n`~/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/`. They auto-load only when\ncwd is `~/DEV` itself — from inside a sub-project, open them by path.\n\nSearch everything with `memsearch search \"<query>\" --top-k 5`."},{"path":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/MEMORY.md","type":"AutoMem","content":"# Memory Index\n\nOne line per memory: title, file, and a hook that says when to open it.\nNever put memory content here — the file itself holds the facts.\n\n- [Printing Press spec traps](project_printing-press-spec-traps.md) — writing a CLI spec: pagination, envelope fields, fixtures, doc regen\n- [zsh shell traps](project_zsh-shell-traps.md) — reserved vars, word-splitting, pipeline exit codes\n- [Status report sourcing](project_status-report-sourcing.md) — which source counts as \"Shipped\", which OKR doc is live\n- [Fireflies CLI on Mac](project_fireflies-cli-broken-on-mac.md) — \"out of memory (14)\", getting transcript text, renames that don't stick\n- [gws Google Forms API](project_gws-forms-api.md) — scopes, create vs batchUpdate, duplicated items\n- [Kenny Boyd doc review](project_kenny-boyd-doc-review-preferences.md) — tone and labelling rules for review docs\n- [Terminal Fluency workspace](project_terminal-fluency-workspace.md) — resume protocol and how he learns CLI\n- [PATH shadowing and cleanup](project_path-shadowing-and-cleanup.md) — measuring PATH honestly; before deleting any binary\n- [Backup/sync system](project_backup-sync-system.md) — manifest routing, verify-by-receipt, schedule history\n- [CFB Analytics Lab](project_cfb-analytics-lab.md) — resume protocol and CFBD API traps\n- [CFB forecast capture](project_cfb-forecast-capture.md) — Big 12 weekly freeze; one wrapper command; is a gap really a missed week?\n- [Drive FUSE rsync loop](project_drive-fuse-rsync-mtime-loop.md) — rsync re-sending identical files to Google Drive\n- [SecondBrain vault location](project_secondbrain-vault-location.md) — current path and what hardcodes it\n- [Milvus lock misdiagnosis](project_milvus-lock-misdiagnosis.md) — Zotero/Milvus errors; diagnose before rebuilding\n- [Memory compiler pipeline](project_memory-compiler-pipeline.md) — dead-flush tells, backfilling a date, \"Indexed 0 chunks\"\n- [memsearch index path drift](project_memsearch-index-path-drift.md) — silent fallback to fewer indexed paths\n- [memsearch hook timeout cap](project_memsearch-hook-timeout-cap.md) — slow or timed-out index; check Mac sleep (`pmset -g log`) first, then corpus growth\n- [Morning briefing retired](project_morning-briefing-retired.md) — where the code, briefings and config went\n- [graphify runtime setup](project_graphify-runtime-setup.md) — venv location, install flags, rebuild triggers\n- [graphify semantic extraction](project_graphify-semantic-extraction.md) — quota traps and silent 429s\n- [Automation cadence](project_automation-cadence.md) — ritual times, reindex, audit due dates, gws/Gmail limits\n- [S2 Cognition analysis](project_s2-cognition-analysis.md) — norms scope, battery size, threshold discipline\n- [Sports teams](user_sports-teams.md) — default team for ambiguous WNBA asks\n- [Working-conditions bottleneck](user_working-conditions-bottleneck.md) — what limits him; the permission gate on acting unasked\n- [Zero-edit YouTube pipeline](reference_zero-edit-youtube-pipeline.md) — Jack Roberts' Claude Code video system\n- [DEV layout and discovery](project_dev-layout-and-discovery.md) — folder rules, depth-2 scan limit, gitignore trap\n- [KeystoneOS verification habits](project_keystoneos-verification-habits.md) — which state claims mislead; re-check before asserting; morning-cadence dies on a `C:\\` or URL `canonicalPath` in projects.json\n- [Portfolio registry provenance](project_portfolio-registry-write-provenance.md) — who writes portfolio.json; how to commit changes\n- [Command centre](project_command-centre.md) — localhost:7373 front door + the /os board, daemon health, backup default-deny\n- [Vendored skill install](project_vendored-skill-install.md) — installing a third-party skill for Claude Code + Codex + Cowork; the `-a` flag trap\n- [Vendored skill repair](project_vendored-skill-repair.md) — a skill returns empty output; which copy is actually live; patches that revert\n- [Personal site build routes](project_personal-site-build-routes.md) — Artifact constraints vs scroll-craft; where the standalone build lives\n- [Book scan page ordering](project_book-scan-page-ordering.md) — phone-scanned book pages out of order; folio OCR lies, read a contact sheet\n- [Ingest review gate](feedback_ingest-review-gate.md) — before ingest-book or any expensive atomization; what the arithmetic gate does and does not catch\n- [Dormant threads](project_dormant-threads.md) — Tezino CampPrep and FaceComps sim: where each stopped and what is still open\n- [RTP CLA course](project_rtp-cla-course.md) — book ingest state, the +13 page offset, the one rebuild still outstanding\n- [ATH Tech framework](project_ath-tech-framework.md) — the shipped 08-14 doc set, the five unwritten gaps, the ITS blocker\n- [Supervisor log pipeline](project_supervisor-log-pipeline.md) — nightly log feeding the Kenny/Chris report; action-items-are-not-outcomes trap\n- [dcg guard blocks](project_dcg-guard-blocks.md) — a Bash command was rejected outright; which shapes trip it and the rewrite that works\n- [Headless tool-deny gap](project_headless-claude-tool-deny-gap.md) — `claude -p --disallowedTools Bash` still runs shell via context-mode MCP; before calling a headless run read-only\n- [Config encoding damage from Windows](project_settings-json-bom-trap.md) — dcg cries \"hook missing\", or the statusline bars render as `â–“` junk; one bad write causes both, in settings.json AND CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md\n- [Tech inventory refresh](project_tech-inventory-refresh.md) — which forms platform is live, why gws cannot pull responses, the stale OneDrive copy, reminder sent 9/8, the refresh command\n- [Brain audit loop](project_brain-audit-loop.md) — scoring the second brain; why manual rituals die and cron ones live\n- [Hook two-copies trap](project_hook-two-copies-trap.md) — a hook patch \"reverts\"; `.claude/hooks/` and `.codex/hooks/` both need it\n- [Child dental plan](user_child-dental-plan.md) — 4yo cavities: pediatric dentist not yet booked, SDF vs n-HAp\n- [ELI5 output style](user_eli5-output-style.md) — concise plain-language output rules shared by Claude Code and Codex\n- [GitHub consolidation](project_github-consolidation.md) — ~/DEV on GitHub: the thin root repo, _ARCHIVE, where DexaProject went, merge traps\n- [Skill bloat and promotion](project_skill-bloat-and-promotion.md) — before touching ANY skill folder: which of the three copies is canonical, why `~/.claude/skills` IS a git repo, the sync script that deletes, the 2026-09-12 audit, the 40 name-only skills (9/14), Pi/pi.dev facts\n- [Prioritization slate](project_prioritization-slate.md) — Eric proposes a new project or idea; the cap, charters, slate-check timer, clearing a nag with mark-done"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"a062d0ab-1198-484e-a9a6-f6e2806d5348","timestamp":"2026-09-25T00:47:38.327Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCodebase and user instructions are shown below. Be sure to adhere to these instructions. IMPORTANT: These instructions OVERRIDE any default behavior and you MUST follow them exactly as written.\n\nContents of /Users/kristinarash/.claude/CLAUDE.md (user's private global instructions for all projects):\n\n# Machine\n\nMachine-specific shell, paths, and traps live in `~/.claude/machine.md` (gitignored; copy `machine.macos.md` or `machine.windows.md` to `machine.md` on a new machine). It is imported below.\n\n@machine.md\n\nTwo machines share this setup: the MacBook (`~/DEV`) and the Baylor Windows laptop (`~/Desktop/DEV`). Projects sync through GitHub (`erash11`), documents through Google Drive. Every project repo carries a Session routine in its `AGENTS.md`: `git pull` + read `docs/STATUS.md` at start; update `STATUS.md`, commit, `git push` at end.\n# Workflow Expectations\n\n- When asked to **create, merge, or consolidate an artifact** (calendar, deck, doc), the expected deliverable is always a produced file. Verify what exists first, then create the artifact regardless — never conclude with \"it already exists\" instead of delivering the file.\n- When the user types `/graphify`, invoke the Skill tool with `skill: \"graphify\"` before doing anything else.\n- Skills are tools, not a gate. Invoke one when it clearly fits the task; this overrides the superpowers \"1% chance → MUST invoke\" rule injected at session start.\n\n# Session Startup\n\nHandled by the `keystone-unified-snapshot.js` SessionStart hook — do not read these files by hand. It injects `global-memory/USER.md`, `global-memory/MEMORY.md`, `transcripts/.errors.log` (only when non-empty), and a pointer to the KeystoneOS snapshot.\n\n- If `.errors.log` content appears, surface it once on the first response, then continue. It is normally empty; entries mean hook failures.\n- If a **\"SessionStart hook could not read a required memory file\"** block appears, say so on the first response instead of working around it.\n- **If no `## User profile` block is in context at session start, the hook did not fire.** Say so, then read `USER.md`, `MEMORY.md` and `transcripts/.errors.log` by hand.\n- What the hook injects is a frozen snapshot. Mid-session writes take effect next session. Never load more than this proactively.\n\n# Memory — routing only\n\nThe two-tier memory system (`~/.claude/global-memory/` and `~/.claude/projects/<slug>/memory/`) is owned by the **`memory-write` skill**, which holds the tier rules, character caps, slug rules, write steps, retrieval ladder, and daily-compiled-log rules.\n\nThe active project's Tier A memory (`~/.claude/projects/<slug>/memory/`, indexed by its `MEMORY.md`) is **auto-injected by the harness** each session. Tier A files are also indexed by memsearch, so they stay recallable across projects.\n\n- Writing a fact — \"remember this\", \"note that\", \"save this\", \"forget about\" → `Skill(\"memory-write\")`\n- Recalling past context — \"did we already…?\", \"what did we decide about X\" → `Skill(\"memory-write\")`, retrieval-ladder section\n- Daily compiled logs at `~/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/daily/` are owned by `claude-memory-compiler`. Never hand-edit them; never read them eagerly.\n- **Slugs differ per machine** (Mac `-Users-kristinarash-DEV-<X>`, Windows `C--Users-eric-rash-Desktop-DEV-<X>`). Tier A written on one is not auto-injected on the other; memsearch still finds it. Durable project facts belong in the repo's `docs/` so both machines see them.\n\nDo not restate the memory procedure in this file. It has one home, and that home is the skill.\n\n---\n\n`AGENTS.md` is the sibling of this file for harnesses that have no Skill tool (Codex and similar). It intentionally carries the memory rules as plain prose instead of routing to a skill. **The two files are not meant to be identical — do not \"fix\" the difference by symlinking them.**\n\nContents of /Users/kristinarash/.claude/machine.md (user's private global instructions for all projects):\n\n# Shell / Environment (macOS)\n\n- zsh/bash is the native surface on this machine. PowerShell 7 (`pwsh`, `/opt/homebrew/bin/pwsh`) is installed only to run the KeystoneOS `.ps1` jobs natively.\n- **The tool-path list has one home: `~/.claude/TOOLPATHS.md`.** Read that file when you need a path. Only the traps below are kept, because acting on them wrongly is expensive.\n- **Verify, don't trust any list.** `which -a <tool>` is authoritative. To read PATH honestly, scrub the environment first:\n  `env -i HOME=\"$HOME\" USER=\"$USER\" TERM=xterm SHELL=/bin/zsh /bin/zsh -lic 'echo $PATH'`\n- Traps:\n  - Python is PEP 668-managed. Use venvs or `uv`, never `pip install` globally.\n  - `uv` is a standalone install at `~/.local/bin/uv`, **not** Homebrew. Claude Code hooks call `$HOME/.local/bin/uv`; do not delete or relocate it.\n  - `timeout` is NOT installed (no GNU coreutils). Don't use it in scripts.\n  - Homebrew owns `/opt/homebrew/bin`. `/usr/local/bin` is empty and stays that way.\n  - Secrets live in the macOS Keychain, not in `~/.zshrc`.\n- DEV projects live at `~/DEV` (not `~/Desktop/DEV`). Workspace map: `~/DEV/CLAUDE.md`.\n- Primary storage drive (documents, data, deliverables): `~/Library/CloudStorage/GoogleDrive-eric.rash11@gmail.com/My Drive/00_Primary_Storage_Drive`.\n\nContents of /Users/kristinarash/DEV/CLAUDE.md (project instructions, checked into the codebase):\n\n# ~/DEV — workspace map\n\nEric Rash — Applied Performance, Baylor Athletics. Sport science and\nfootball analytics, plus the agent system that runs them.\n\nThis file is a **map, not a rulebook**. Behavior rules live in\n`~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`. Read only the index you need.\n\n## Areas\n\n| Area | Index | What lives there |\n|---|---|---|\n| Football | `FOOTBALL.md` | Game film, player analytics, CFB prediction. ~39k files — about two thirds of DEV. |\n| Performance | `PERFORMANCE.md` | Athlete monitoring, testing, load, risk. GPS, force plate, VALD, DEXA, S2. |\n| Research | `RESEARCH.md` | Literature, Zotero, book library, reading pipelines. |\n| Platform | `PLATFORM.md` | KeystoneOS, dashboards, CLIs, scheduled jobs. |\n| Program | `PROGRAM.md` | Staff reporting, curriculum, proposals, vetting, brand. |\n| Personal | `PERSONAL.md` | Side projects. Not Baylor work. |\n| Commands | `COMMANDS.md` | Desk reference: every report/project command Eric can run himself. |\n\n## Elsewhere on disk\n\n| Path | What it is |\n|---|---|\n| `~/DEV/_ARCHIVE/` | Parked projects. Not a git repo, so the consolidation sweep skips it. Has its own `README.md`. |\n| `~/DEV/_INBOX/` | Loose files from the `~/DEV` root. Own repo. |\n| `~/SecondBrain/` | Obsidian vault, ~850 notes. Own `CLAUDE.md`. |\n| `~/.claude/skills/` | ~155 skills |\n| `~/go/bin/` | 8 custom CLIs built with `cli-printing-press` |\n| `~/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/knowledge/` | ~230 compiled articles |\n\n## Layout rules\n\nFull rules — grouping depth, the depth-2 discovery limit, and the gitignored-subtree\ntrap — live in project memory: `project_dev-layout-and-discovery.md`.\n\n- 23 projects carry their own `CLAUDE.md`. Read it before working in one.\n\n## Handling care\n\n- `DexaProject/` holds identifiable health data. It lives on Google Drive, not in\n  `~/DEV`, on **both** machines — one copy, reached by each machine's own path:\n  - Mac: `~/Library/CloudStorage/GoogleDrive-eric.rash11@gmail.com/My Drive/00_Primary_Storage_Drive/DexaProject`\n  - Windows: `G:\\My Drive\\00_Primary_Storage_Drive\\DexaProject`\n\n  See `PERFORMANCE.md`.\n  Never paste its contents into chat, an artifact, or an external service.\n\n## Keeping this true\n\nWhen a file moves or a new project starts, **update the router in the same\nturn**. A stale pointer is worse than no pointer.\n\nThe counts above are approximate on purpose — they convey scale, not state, and\na `~` keeps ordinary growth from making this file wrong. Re-measure them only\nwhen one is off by enough to change a decision. Counts last checked 2026-09-05.\n\nMemory files named in these indexes (`project_*.md`, `user_*.md`) live at\n`~/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/`. They auto-load only when\ncwd is `~/DEV` itself — from inside a sub-project, open them by path.\n\nSearch everything with `memsearch search \"<query>\" --top-k 5`.\n\nContents of /Users/kristinarash/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/MEMORY.md (user's auto-memory, persists across conversations):\n\n# Memory Index\n\nOne line per memory: title, file, and a hook that says when to open it.\nNever put memory content here — the file itself holds the facts.\n\n- [Printing Press spec traps](project_printing-press-spec-traps.md) — writing a CLI spec: pagination, envelope fields, fixtures, doc regen\n- [zsh shell traps](project_zsh-shell-traps.md) — reserved vars, word-splitting, pipeline exit codes\n- [Status report sourcing](project_status-report-sourcing.md) — which source counts as \"Shipped\", which OKR doc is live\n- [Fireflies CLI on Mac](project_fireflies-cli-broken-on-mac.md) — \"out of memory (14)\", getting transcript text, renames that don't stick\n- [gws Google Forms API](project_gws-forms-api.md) — scopes, create vs batchUpdate, duplicated items\n- [Kenny Boyd doc review](project_kenny-boyd-doc-review-preferences.md) — tone and labelling rules for review docs\n- [Terminal Fluency workspace](project_terminal-fluency-workspace.md) — resume protocol and how he learns CLI\n- [PATH shadowing and cleanup](project_path-shadowing-and-cleanup.md) — measuring PATH honestly; before deleting any binary\n- [Backup/sync system](project_backup-sync-system.md) — manifest routing, verify-by-receipt, schedule history\n- [CFB Analytics Lab](project_cfb-analytics-lab.md) — resume protocol and CFBD API traps\n- [CFB forecast capture](project_cfb-forecast-capture.md) — Big 12 weekly freeze; one wrapper command; is a gap really a missed week?\n- [Drive FUSE rsync loop](project_drive-fuse-rsync-mtime-loop.md) — rsync re-sending identical files to Google Drive\n- [SecondBrain vault location](project_secondbrain-vault-location.md) — current path and what hardcodes it\n- [Milvus lock misdiagnosis](project_milvus-lock-misdiagnosis.md) — Zotero/Milvus errors; diagnose before rebuilding\n- [Memory compiler pipeline](project_memory-compiler-pipeline.md) — dead-flush tells, backfilling a date, \"Indexed 0 chunks\"\n- [memsearch index path drift](project_memsearch-index-path-drift.md) — silent fallback to fewer indexed paths\n- [memsearch hook timeout cap](project_memsearch-hook-timeout-cap.md) — slow or timed-out index; check Mac sleep (`pmset -g log`) first, then corpus growth\n- [Morning briefing retired](project_morning-briefing-retired.md) — where the code, briefings and config went\n- [graphify runtime setup](project_graphify-runtime-setup.md) — venv location, install flags, rebuild triggers\n- [graphify semantic extraction](project_graphify-semantic-extraction.md) — quota traps and silent 429s\n- [Automation cadence](project_automation-cadence.md) — ritual times, reindex, audit due dates, gws/Gmail limits\n- [S2 Cognition analysis](project_s2-cognition-analysis.md) — norms scope, battery size, threshold discipline\n- [Sports teams](user_sports-teams.md) — default team for ambiguous WNBA asks\n- [Working-conditions bottleneck](user_working-conditions-bottleneck.md) — what limits him; the permission gate on acting unasked\n- [Zero-edit YouTube pipeline](reference_zero-edit-youtube-pipeline.md) — Jack Roberts' Claude Code video system\n- [DEV layout and discovery](project_dev-layout-and-discovery.md) — folder rules, depth-2 scan limit, gitignore trap\n- [KeystoneOS verification habits](project_keystoneos-verification-habits.md) — which state claims mislead; re-check before asserting; morning-cadence dies on a `C:\\` or URL `canonicalPath` in projects.json\n- [Portfolio registry provenance](project_portfolio-registry-write-provenance.md) — who writes portfolio.json; how to commit changes\n- [Command centre](project_command-centre.md) — localhost:7373 front door + the /os board, daemon health, backup default-deny\n- [Vendored skill install](project_vendored-skill-install.md) — installing a third-party skill for Claude Code + Codex + Cowork; the `-a` flag trap\n- [Vendored skill repair](project_vendored-skill-repair.md) — a skill returns empty output; which copy is actually live; patches that revert\n- [Personal site build routes](project_personal-site-build-routes.md) — Artifact constraints vs scroll-craft; where the standalone build lives\n- [Book scan page ordering](project_book-scan-page-ordering.md) — phone-scanned book pages out of order; folio OCR lies, read a contact sheet\n- [Ingest review gate](feedback_ingest-review-gate.md) — before ingest-book or any expensive atomization; what the arithmetic gate does and does not catch\n- [Dormant threads](project_dormant-threads.md) — Tezino CampPrep and FaceComps sim: where each stopped and what is still open\n- [RTP CLA course](project_rtp-cla-course.md) — book ingest state, the +13 page offset, the one rebuild still outstanding\n- [ATH Tech framework](project_ath-tech-framework.md) — the shipped 08-14 doc set, the five unwritten gaps, the ITS blocker\n- [Supervisor log pipeline](project_supervisor-log-pipeline.md) — nightly log feeding the Kenny/Chris report; action-items-are-not-outcomes trap\n- [dcg guard blocks](project_dcg-guard-blocks.md) — a Bash command was rejected outright; which shapes trip it and the rewrite that works\n- [Headless tool-deny gap](project_headless-claude-tool-deny-gap.md) — `claude -p --disallowedTools Bash` still runs shell via context-mode MCP; before calling a headless run read-only\n- [Config encoding damage from Windows](project_settings-json-bom-trap.md) — dcg cries \"hook missing\", or the statusline bars render as `â–“` junk; one bad write causes both, in settings.json AND CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md\n- [Tech inventory refresh](project_tech-inventory-refresh.md) — which forms platform is live, why gws cannot pull responses, the stale OneDrive copy, reminder sent 9/8, the refresh command\n- [Brain audit loop](project_brain-audit-loop.md) — scoring the second brain; why manual rituals die and cron ones live\n- [Hook two-copies trap](project_hook-two-copies-trap.md) — a hook patch \"reverts\"; `.claude/hooks/` and `.codex/hooks/` both need it\n- [Child dental plan](user_child-dental-plan.md) — 4yo cavities: pediatric dentist not yet booked, SDF vs n-HAp\n- [ELI5 output style](user_eli5-output-style.md) — concise plain-language output rules shared by Claude Code and Codex\n- [GitHub consolidation](project_github-consolidation.md) — ~/DEV on GitHub: the thin root repo, _ARCHIVE, where DexaProject went, merge traps\n- [Skill bloat and promotion](project_skill-bloat-and-promotion.md) — before touching ANY skill folder: which of the three copies is canonical, why `~/.claude/skills` IS a git repo, the sync script that deletes, the 2026-09-12 audit, the 40 name-only skills (9/14), Pi/pi.dev facts\n- [Prioritization slate](project_prioritization-slate.md) — Eric proposes a new project or idea; the cap, charters, slate-check timer, clearing a nag with mark-done\n</system-reminder>"}],"session_id":"51d890bb-1aa4-4397-9981-be25e2430651","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"51d890bb-1aa4-4397-9981-be25e2430651","version":"2.1.281","gitBranch":"main"}
