{"parentUuid":"74afb587-a06c-41ea-9eec-4373625399e6","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ddcedd82-46d8-49d9-a69d-e2f38c6686bd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0186uLtMP81LbtBu2zLfZM52","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# STATUS\n2\t\n3\tRead this first. Update it before ending every session.\n4\t\n5\tLast updated 2026-09-13 (Mac, background session). Evidence for every claim below is in\n6\t`docs/audits/2026-09-12-gate-a-approval.md`.\n7\t\n8\t## Current state\n9\t- **2026-09-24 (Windows): Windows is the daytime machine, the Mac the evening one.** Two changes follow. First, the ritual nudges move to Windows: `ritual-check.ps1` has a `msg.exe` branch again, and its path defaults now follow the OS, because Mac-only paths made every ritual read \"never run\" on Windows. Enable `KeystoneOS-Rituals` on Windows and boot out `com.keystone.rituals` on the Mac. Second, `daily-backup` in `data/jobs.json` moves to 21:00 (makeup window 21:00-23:59), so the 07:00 reconcile no longer re-runs it. The CRASHBOX SSD layer only captures if the drive is attached at 21:00.\n10\t- **2026-09-14: `ritual-check.ps1` gained a `slate` ritual.** It runs `~/DEV/project-triage/portfolio.py slate-check --json` (job-lane prioritization rules: cap, charters, dated steps, OKR checkpoints) and reports DUE, never OK, if the check cannot run. Tests: `tests/keystone-ritual-slate.ps1`; `keystone-ritual-forecast-capture.ps1` now expects 5 rituals.\n11\t- **2026-09-14: Friday ritual runs also write `SecondBrain/Inbox/weekly-slate/YYYY-MM-DD.md`** via `portfolio.py week-report` (DUE if it cannot write). Handoff: `~/DEV/project-triage/docs/handoffs/2026-09-14-prioritization-system.md`.\n12\t- The dominant thread is the **harness-agnostic AIOS plan**:\n13\t  `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md` (approved; do not edit —\n14\t  its SHA-256 `71b5242e…` binds the approval). Goal: every skill Eric owns loads\n15\t  identically in Claude Code, Codex and Pi from one versioned canonical folder, plus a\n16\t  recurring audit that keeps the AIOS from rotting.\n17\t- Architecture: `~/.claude/skills/` (repo `erash11/claude-skills`) is canonical and holds\n18\t  real directories only. `~/.agents/skills/` and `~/.codex/skills/` are generated views\n19\t  rebuilt per machine by `sync-to-codex.sh` / `.ps1` — symlinks on Mac, copies on Windows.\n20\t- **Tasks 1–7 done.** Task 8 (Pi trial) **PAUSED by Eric** (2026-09-13). It also needs\n21\t  `sudo` to create `piuser`. Report and unblock commands: `docs/audits/2026-09-12-pi-trial.md`.\n22\t- **Roster resolved 2026-09-13 (Option B):** the 7 owned skills are on again in Claude Code\n23\t  (`~/.claude` commit `21c686d`). Checker: 42/42 portable.\n24\t- **First `aios-audit` ran 2026-09-13:** `docs/audits/aios-audit-2026-09-13.md`. Two RED:\n25\t  the Codex snapshot hook is a stale copy, and the GPS feed looks frozen since 2026-08-01.\n26\t- **Gate B** (2 rounds), **Gate C** (2 rounds) and two final Codex verification rounds\n27\t  (3 and 4, `gpt-5.6-terra`) ran on 2026-09-12/13. Every code finding is fixed: C-01 exec\n28\t  bits, C-02 atomic stale-lock reclaim, C-03 usage metrics scoped to Claude transcripts,\n29\t  IR-01 list/map names rejected, IR-03 implicit null/boolean/number/timestamp rejected,\n30\t  IR-04/IR-05 exact YAML grammars (`0008` kept as a number on purpose: YAML 1.2 core).\n31\t  Round 5 (last) returned REVISE on `62fbb72` with IR-06/IR-07; host checks show both hold only\n32\t  for the npm `yaml` library's 1.1 mode, not PyYAML or YAML 1.2 core. **Eric accepted the\n33\t  checker as is (2026-09-13):** the contract is PyYAML + YAML 1.2 core. Closed.\n34\t- **Audit build 1 done (2026-09-13):** Codex snapshot hook synced to the 98-line copy;\n35\t  `memory-write` and `project_backup-sync-system.md` now say both machines are active\n36\t  (`~/.claude/skills` `cd86eff`, `~/.claude` `532a0d3`).\n37\t- Monthly metrics run on launchd `com.keystone.aiosaudit` (day 1, 14:00). It writes a row\n38\t  to `docs/audits/aios-trend.md` and a nudge; it never commits.\n39\t- `portability_failures=0` since the roster decision (2026-09-13). Every layout invariant is 0.\n40\t\n41\t## Next\n42\t- **Audit build 2 (GPS):** option A approved 2026-09-13 — `docs/audits/2026-09-13-gps-locations.md`.\n43\t  Auburn JSON moved to GD and untracked (done). Three old copies proven duplicate; Eric deletes\n44\t  them by hand (the permission guard blocked Claude). **Regular pull built and live 2026-09-13:**\n45\t  DB backfilled to 2026-09-12 (713 sessions), launchd `com.keystone.gpspull` at 06:30, alerts to\n46\t  `.errors.log`. Details: `~/DEV/DataBase_GPS_Reporting/docs/STATUS.md`. Storage rule: Google Drive\n47\t  only; OneDrive dropped.\n48\t- Other audit proposals (vault note rot, double `dcg` registration, stale router counts,\n49\t  `measure.sh` sort bug): see `docs/audits/aios-audit-2026-09-13.md`.\n50\t- **Task 8 (Pi trial):** paused by Eric.\n51\t\n52\t## Open questions\n53\t- GPS: Eric turns off the GPS step in Windows `Refresh_All_Data` (the Mac now owns the DB).\n54\t  Three old GPS copies still to delete by hand (paths in `docs/audits/2026-09-13-gps-locations.md`).\n55\t- Backup manifest still routes to OneDrive `Backups/DEV-NonRepo`; OneDrive is dropped.\n56\t\n57\t## Gotchas\n58\t- Never commit a symlink into `~/.claude/skills/`. Windows pulls that repo and an absolute\n59\t  Mac symlink arrives unusable. A pre-commit hook refuses it.\n60\t- Hooks and sync scripts exist in two copies (`~/.claude/hooks/`, `~/.codex/hooks/`; `.sh`\n61\t  and `.ps1`). Any change patches both.\n62\t- Never run `graphify install --platform agents`: the views link into canonical, so it\n63\t  overwrites the Claude variant. Use `--platform claude` only.\n64\t- `never_used` in the metrics is **Claude Code evidence only**. Check `~/.codex/sessions`\n65\t  before recommending any deletion.\n66\t- `claude -p --disallowedTools Bash` does not block the context-mode MCP shell tools.\n67\t- A concurrent `closeout` commits whatever is uncommitted. Commit at each verified step.\n68\t- **Never commit to a repo while a `claudex-loop` inspection of it is running.** The runner\n69\t  snapshots the tree and marks the run `failed` (\"Code changed during inspection\").\n70\t  Happened in round 5 on 2026-09-13.\n71\t- `dcg` blocks: `rm -rf` in heredocs, `mv` and `>` redirects on home paths, `git` inside\n72\t  command substitution. Use the Write tool plus a Python file that does the I/O.\n73\t- Never point Pi at `~/DEV` — it ships no sandbox and no approval prompts, by design.\n74\t- Never let any harness near `DexaProject` (identifiable athlete health data, on Google\n75\t  Drive, not in `~/DEV`).\n76\t- Plugin skills (`superpowers`, `mattpocock-skills`) are vendored and out of scope.\n77\t- On the Mac: `timeout` is not installed and Python is PEP 668-managed (stdlib `python3`\n78\t  or `uv`, never global `pip install`).\n79\t- No success claim without pasted command output.\n80\t"}]},"uuid":"17513b4f-3e0c-4a5b-8fe1-92c2bcfec6a3","timestamp":"2026-09-25T00:57:41.038Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/STATUS.md","content":"# STATUS\n\nRead this first. Update it before ending every session.\n\nLast updated 2026-09-13 (Mac, background session). Evidence for every claim below is in\n`docs/audits/2026-09-12-gate-a-approval.md`.\n\n## Current state\n- **2026-09-24 (Windows): Windows is the daytime machine, the Mac the evening one.** Two changes follow. First, the ritual nudges move to Windows: `ritual-check.ps1` has a `msg.exe` branch again, and its path defaults now follow the OS, because Mac-only paths made every ritual read \"never run\" on Windows. Enable `KeystoneOS-Rituals` on Windows and boot out `com.keystone.rituals` on the Mac. Second, `daily-backup` in `data/jobs.json` moves to 21:00 (makeup window 21:00-23:59), so the 07:00 reconcile no longer re-runs it. The CRASHBOX SSD layer only captures if the drive is attached at 21:00.\n- **2026-09-14: `ritual-check.ps1` gained a `slate` ritual.** It runs `~/DEV/project-triage/portfolio.py slate-check --json` (job-lane prioritization rules: cap, charters, dated steps, OKR checkpoints) and reports DUE, never OK, if the check cannot run. Tests: `tests/keystone-ritual-slate.ps1`; `keystone-ritual-forecast-capture.ps1` now expects 5 rituals.\n- **2026-09-14: Friday ritual runs also write `SecondBrain/Inbox/weekly-slate/YYYY-MM-DD.md`** via `portfolio.py week-report` (DUE if it cannot write). Handoff: `~/DEV/project-triage/docs/handoffs/2026-09-14-prioritization-system.md`.\n- The dominant thread is the **harness-agnostic AIOS plan**:\n  `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md` (approved; do not edit —\n  its SHA-256 `71b5242e…` binds the approval). Goal: every skill Eric owns loads\n  identically in Claude Code, Codex and Pi from one versioned canonical folder, plus a\n  recurring audit that keeps the AIOS from rotting.\n- Architecture: `~/.claude/skills/` (repo `erash11/claude-skills`) is canonical and holds\n  real directories only. `~/.agents/skills/` and `~/.codex/skills/` are generated views\n  rebuilt per machine by `sync-to-codex.sh` / `.ps1` — symlinks on Mac, copies on Windows.\n- **Tasks 1–7 done.** Task 8 (Pi trial) **PAUSED by Eric** (2026-09-13). It also needs\n  `sudo` to create `piuser`. Report and unblock commands: `docs/audits/2026-09-12-pi-trial.md`.\n- **Roster resolved 2026-09-13 (Option B):** the 7 owned skills are on again in Claude Code\n  (`~/.claude` commit `21c686d`). Checker: 42/42 portable.\n- **First `aios-audit` ran 2026-09-13:** `docs/audits/aios-audit-2026-09-13.md`. Two RED:\n  the Codex snapshot hook is a stale copy, and the GPS feed looks frozen since 2026-08-01.\n- **Gate B** (2 rounds), **Gate C** (2 rounds) and two final Codex verification rounds\n  (3 and 4, `gpt-5.6-terra`) ran on 2026-09-12/13. Every code finding is fixed: C-01 exec\n  bits, C-02 atomic stale-lock reclaim, C-03 usage metrics scoped to Claude transcripts,\n  IR-01 list/map names rejected, IR-03 implicit null/boolean/number/timestamp rejected,\n  IR-04/IR-05 exact YAML grammars (`0008` kept as a number on purpose: YAML 1.2 core).\n  Round 5 (last) returned REVISE on `62fbb72` with IR-06/IR-07; host checks show both hold only\n  for the npm `yaml` library's 1.1 mode, not PyYAML or YAML 1.2 core. **Eric accepted the\n  checker as is (2026-09-13):** the contract is PyYAML + YAML 1.2 core. Closed.\n- **Audit build 1 done (2026-09-13):** Codex snapshot hook synced to the 98-line copy;\n  `memory-write` and `project_backup-sync-system.md` now say both machines are active\n  (`~/.claude/skills` `cd86eff`, `~/.claude` `532a0d3`).\n- Monthly metrics run on launchd `com.keystone.aiosaudit` (day 1, 14:00). It writes a row\n  to `docs/audits/aios-trend.md` and a nudge; it never commits.\n- `portability_failures=0` since the roster decision (2026-09-13). Every layout invariant is 0.\n\n## Next\n- **Audit build 2 (GPS):** option A approved 2026-09-13 — `docs/audits/2026-09-13-gps-locations.md`.\n  Auburn JSON moved to GD and untracked (done). Three old copies proven duplicate; Eric deletes\n  them by hand (the permission guard blocked Claude). **Regular pull built and live 2026-09-13:**\n  DB backfilled to 2026-09-12 (713 sessions), launchd `com.keystone.gpspull` at 06:30, alerts to\n  `.errors.log`. Details: `~/DEV/DataBase_GPS_Reporting/docs/STATUS.md`. Storage rule: Google Drive\n  only; OneDrive dropped.\n- Other audit proposals (vault note rot, double `dcg` registration, stale router counts,\n  `measure.sh` sort bug): see `docs/audits/aios-audit-2026-09-13.md`.\n- **Task 8 (Pi trial):** paused by Eric.\n\n## Open questions\n- GPS: Eric turns off the GPS step in Windows `Refresh_All_Data` (the Mac now owns the DB).\n  Three old GPS copies still to delete by hand (paths in `docs/audits/2026-09-13-gps-locations.md`).\n- Backup manifest still routes to OneDrive `Backups/DEV-NonRepo`; OneDrive is dropped.\n\n## Gotchas\n- Never commit a symlink into `~/.claude/skills/`. Windows pulls that repo and an absolute\n  Mac symlink arrives unusable. A pre-commit hook refuses it.\n- Hooks and sync scripts exist in two copies (`~/.claude/hooks/`, `~/.codex/hooks/`; `.sh`\n  and `.ps1`). Any change patches both.\n- Never run `graphify install --platform agents`: the views link into canonical, so it\n  overwrites the Claude variant. Use `--platform claude` only.\n- `never_used` in the metrics is **Claude Code evidence only**. Check `~/.codex/sessions`\n  before recommending any deletion.\n- `claude -p --disallowedTools Bash` does not block the context-mode MCP shell tools.\n- A concurrent `closeout` commits whatever is uncommitted. Commit at each verified step.\n- **Never commit to a repo while a `claudex-loop` inspection of it is running.** The runner\n  snapshots the tree and marks the run `failed` (\"Code changed during inspection\").\n  Happened in round 5 on 2026-09-13.\n- `dcg` blocks: `rm -rf` in heredocs, `mv` and `>` redirects on home paths, `git` inside\n  command substitution. Use the Write tool plus a Python file that does the I/O.\n- Never point Pi at `~/DEV` — it ships no sandbox and no approval prompts, by design.\n- Never let any harness near `DexaProject` (identifiable athlete health data, on Google\n  Drive, not in `~/DEV`).\n- Plugin skills (`superpowers`, `mattpocock-skills`) are vendored and out of scope.\n- On the Mac: `timeout` is not installed and Python is PEP 668-managed (stdlib `python3`\n  or `uv`, never global `pip install`).\n- No success claim without pasted command output.\n","numLines":80,"startLine":1,"totalLines":80}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"74afb587-a06c-41ea-9eec-4373625399e6","session_id":"51d890bb-1aa4-4397-9981-be25e2430651","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"51d890bb-1aa4-4397-9981-be25e2430651","version":"2.1.281","gitBranch"