{"parentUuid":"c1c4b318-3a48-4b18-96b3-001a7f54e41f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ddcedd82-46d8-49d9-a69d-e2f38c6686bd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018yQLytnvxoLVefqqLfsiwG","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# KeystoneOS Router\n2\t\n3\tYou are operating inside KeystoneOS, Eric's cross-harness control plane for project context, memory, Graphify maps, Obsidian synthesis, and daily execution. This file is canonical for all harnesses and answers \"where does X live?\" in one hop.\n4\t\n5\t## Where things live\n6\t\n7\t| Need | Go to |\n8\t|---|---|\n9\t| Active project registry (human) | `projects/registry.md` |\n10\t| Project key list (machine) | `data/projects.json` |\n11\t| Resume brief for project X | `projects/active/<Key>.md` |\n12\t| Memory sources, all harnesses | `data/memory-sources.json` |\n13\t| Memory retrieval policy | `memory/retrieval-policy.md` |\n14\t| Memory index path templates | `data/memory-index-paths.json` |\n15\t| Memory query | `.\\scripts\\keystone.ps1 memory <terms> [-Scope fast|broad]` |\n16\t| Inventory scan roots/config | `data/discovery-roots.json` |\n17\t| Managed scheduled jobs (registry) | `data/jobs.json` |\n18\t| Did a job actually run today? | `.\\scripts\\keystone-reconcile.ps1 -DryRun -Json`, or `Test-JobCompleteOn` — **not** `run-ledger.json` alone, and never the scheduler's own history |\n19\t| Per-run job output | `outputs/jobs/<job>-<date>.{out,err}.log` |\n20\t| Decisions + rationale | `decisions/log.md` |\n21\t| Standing cross-harness rules | `context/standing-rules.md` |\n22\t| Issue tracker (per-feature) | `.scratch/<feature>/` — see `docs/agents/issue-tracker.md` |\n23\t| Reachable systems + how to verify | `connections.md` |\n24\t| OS drift/freshness audits | `audits/os-audit-*.md` (run the `os-audit` skill) |\n25\t| Operating principles, priorities, voice | `context/*.md` |\n26\t| SecondBrain vault (human synthesis) | `C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\SecondBrain` |\n27\t| Knowledge frameworks | `SecondBrain\\Knowledge\\frameworks\\` |\n28\t| Consult a book advisor (\"ask my <domain> advisor\") | `advisor` skill; grounded in `SecondBrain\\Knowledge\\library\\`, personas in `…\\library\\advisors\\` |\n29\t| Ingest a book into the advisor library | `ingest-book` skill; drop the PDF/EPUB in `DEV\\BookInbox\\` |\n30\t| Review library coverage / gaps | `library-review` skill |\n31\t| Workflows (daily/weekly rituals) | `workflows/*.md` |\n32\t| Generated outputs (morning, plan, brief, closeout, context, inventory, intake) | `outputs/<kind>/<date>*.md` |\n33\t| Dashboard | `outputs/dashboard/index.html` |\n34\t| Morning cockpit (OKR-driven) | `outputs/dashboard/cockpit.html` (regenerated by `cockpit` / `today` / morning cadence) |\n35\t| OKR source of truth | `SecondBrain\\Projects\\okr-tracker\\` (`okrs.yaml` + generated `okrs.json`); link projects with `okr-link` |\n36\t| Graph maps | `<project-repo>\\graphify-out`; registry at `graphify/registry.md`; Obsidian bridge at `SecondBrain\\Projects\\Graphify\\<Key>\\GRAPHIFY_SYNC.md` |\n37\t| Verification expectations | `verification/default-checklist.md` |\n38\t| Specs and plans | `docs/superpowers/specs/` and `docs/superpowers/plans/` |\n39\t| Test suites | `tests/*.ps1` |\n40\t| Codex memory bridge | `docs/codex-memory-bridge.md`, hooks in `scripts/codex-hooks/` |\n41\t| agy CLI memory bridge | `docs/agy-memory-bridge.md`, `scripts/agy-sync.ps1` |\n42\t\n43\t## Commands — `.\\scripts\\keystone.ps1 <command>`\n44\t\n45\t`today` · `morning` · `projects` · `resume <Key>` · `context <Key>` · `paths` · `health` · `heal [<Key>]` · `freshness [-Sweep]` · `memory <terms> [-Scope fast|broad]` · `graphify` · `graphsync <Key>` · `status` · `where <Key>` · `start <Key>` · `brief <Key>` · `plan` · `closeout <Key>` · `open <Key>` · `inventory` · `intake` · `promote <path>` · `dashboard` · `cockpit` · `okr-link <Key> <KR-id>` · `agy-sync` · `meeting-sync` · `snapshot`\n46\t\n47\t`health` answers \"do the paths resolve?\" — `freshness` answers \"are the hand-written claims still true?\" The second is the one that decays silently; it runs automatically in the morning cadence.\n48\t\n49\t`.\\scripts\\ritual-check.ps1 [-Notify|-Json]` reports overdue rituals (`/interview-me`, `/weekly-review`). Runs in the morning cadence, and the `KeystoneOS-Rituals` task nudges on weekdays at 17:00 and Fridays at 15:30.\n50\t\n51\t## Scheduled job durability\n52\t\n53\tManaged jobs are declared in `data/jobs.json` and started **only** through `.\\scripts\\run-job.ps1 -Job <id>`, which takes a per-job lock, enforces a timeout, and records the outcome to `outputs/run-ledger.json`. `.\\scripts\\keystone-reconcile.ps1 [-DryRun] [-Json]` re-runs anything with no success recorded for today; the `KeystoneOS-Reconcile` task fires it at logon (+5m) and hourly.\n54\t\n55\tThe rule this encodes: **a scheduled task exiting is not evidence the work happened.** Ask the ledger, or a job's own log via its `successProbe` — never `Get-ScheduledTaskInfo`. On 2026-07-27 the scheduler reported the morning cadence had \"successfully completed\" with a return code that actually meant the process was killed mid-run. See `decisions/log.md` 2026-07-27 and `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-27-scheduled-job-durability-design.md`.\n56\t\n57\tRe-run `.\\scripts\\install-reconcile-task.ps1 -Apply` and `.\\scripts\\harden-scheduled-tasks.ps1 -Apply` after changing task wiring; both are idempotent and dry-run by default.\n58\t\n59\tFront door: when the user says \"work on X\" / \"let's do X\" / \"resume X\", run `.\\scripts\\keystone.ps1 context <X>` FIRST. It resolves the path (self-healing), shows live git, inlines the brief, points at the project's own CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md, and surfaces memory hits + recent decisions — full context in one hop before acting. Paths self-heal on read; `heal` persists a corrected path (auto-commits).\n60\t\n61\tNew project into KeystoneOS: `inventory` → `intake` → `promote <path-or-name> -Status \"Active\"` (writes brief + registry row + projects.json). Map, don't copy — see `decisions/log.md` 2026-06-11.\n62\t\n63\t## Precedence — what wins when two places disagree\n64\t\n65\tRead this before trusting any single file. Two stores disagreeing is the most common way this OS gives a wrong answer.\n66\t\n67\t1. **`AGENTS.md` is the source of truth for routing.** `README.md` and `CLAUDE.md`/`GEMINI.md` defer to it. If they disagree with this table, this table is right and they are stale.\n68\t2. **Generated beats hand-written.** `data/*.json` and anything under `outputs/` beat any `.md` prose describing the same registry. `data/projects.json` beats `projects/registry.md`; `data/memory-sources.json` beats any narrative list of sources.\n69\t3. **Live check beats recorded state.** Any claim about whether a tool is reachable or authenticated (`connections.md`, tool notes) is a hint, not a fact. Run the check command before acting on it.\n70\t4. **Root beats worktree.** `.claude/worktrees/` holds full copies of this repo at older commits. If a search returns two versions of a file, the one at the repo root wins. Never cite a worktree copy as current.\n71\t5. **`decisions/log.md` is the decision record.** Newest entry wins on any conflict with older prose elsewhere.\n72\t\n73\t## Operating rules\n74\t\n75\t- KeystoneOS is a map and control plane, not the source repo for every project.\n76\t- Do not copy large project files into KeystoneOS. Prefer links and local paths to canonical sources.\n77\t- Before multi-step work, find or write a spec (`docs/superpowers/specs/`).\n78\t- Before claiming completion, state and run the verification plan (`verification/default-checklist.md`).\n79\t- Preserve the existing Claude and Codex memory systems; integrate by reading/querying, not overwriting.\n80\t- Use Graphify for comprehension when a repo or corpus is too large to reread directly.\n81\t\n82\t## Harness adapters\n83\t\n84\t`CLAUDE.md` (Claude) and `GEMINI.md` (Gemini) are thin adapters that point here. Keep the three files in sync: shared policy lives in this file only.\n85\t\n86\t## Session routine\n87\t- Start: run `git pull`, then read docs/STATUS.md before doing anything else.\n88\t- End: update docs/STATUS.md (done, next, open questions), commit, and `git push`.\n89\t- Never leave uncommitted work at the end of a session.\n90\t"}]},"uuid":"78576fa5-4293-443c-b912-8c00e962dff7","timestamp":"2026-09-25T00:57:41.400Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/AGENTS.md","content":"# KeystoneOS Router\n\nYou are operating inside KeystoneOS, Eric's cross-harness control plane for project context, memory, Graphify maps, Obsidian synthesis, and daily execution. This file is canonical for all harnesses and answers \"where does X live?\" in one hop.\n\n## Where things live\n\n| Need | Go to |\n|---|---|\n| Active project registry (human) | `projects/registry.md` |\n| Project key list (machine) | `data/projects.json` |\n| Resume brief for project X | `projects/active/<Key>.md` |\n| Memory sources, all harnesses | `data/memory-sources.json` |\n| Memory retrieval policy | `memory/retrieval-policy.md` |\n| Memory index path templates | `data/memory-index-paths.json` |\n| Memory query | `.\\scripts\\keystone.ps1 memory <terms> [-Scope fast|broad]` |\n| Inventory scan roots/config | `data/discovery-roots.json` |\n| Managed scheduled jobs (registry) | `data/jobs.json` |\n| Did a job actually run today? | `.\\scripts\\keystone-reconcile.ps1 -DryRun -Json`, or `Test-JobCompleteOn` — **not** `run-ledger.json` alone, and never the scheduler's own history |\n| Per-run job output | `outputs/jobs/<job>-<date>.{out,err}.log` |\n| Decisions + rationale | `decisions/log.md` |\n| Standing cross-harness rules | `context/standing-rules.md` |\n| Issue tracker (per-feature) | `.scratch/<feature>/` — see `docs/agents/issue-tracker.md` |\n| Reachable systems + how to verify | `connections.md` |\n| OS drift/freshness audits | `audits/os-audit-*.md` (run the `os-audit` skill) |\n| Operating principles, priorities, voice | `context/*.md` |\n| SecondBrain vault (human synthesis) | `C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\SecondBrain` |\n| Knowledge frameworks | `SecondBrain\\Knowledge\\frameworks\\` |\n| Consult a book advisor (\"ask my <domain> advisor\") | `advisor` skill; grounded in `SecondBrain\\Knowledge\\library\\`, personas in `…\\library\\advisors\\` |\n| Ingest a book into the advisor library | `ingest-book` skill; drop the PDF/EPUB in `DEV\\BookInbox\\` |\n| Review library coverage / gaps | `library-review` skill |\n| Workflows (daily/weekly rituals) | `workflows/*.md` |\n| Generated outputs (morning, plan, brief, closeout, context, inventory, intake) | `outputs/<kind>/<date>*.md` |\n| Dashboard | `outputs/dashboard/index.html` |\n| Morning cockpit (OKR-driven) | `outputs/dashboard/cockpit.html` (regenerated by `cockpit` / `today` / morning cadence) |\n| OKR source of truth | `SecondBrain\\Projects\\okr-tracker\\` (`okrs.yaml` + generated `okrs.json`); link projects with `okr-link` |\n| Graph maps | `<project-repo>\\graphify-out`; registry at `graphify/registry.md`; Obsidian bridge at `SecondBrain\\Projects\\Graphify\\<Key>\\GRAPHIFY_SYNC.md` |\n| Verification expectations | `verification/default-checklist.md` |\n| Specs and plans | `docs/superpowers/specs/` and `docs/superpowers/plans/` |\n| Test suites | `tests/*.ps1` |\n| Codex memory bridge | `docs/codex-memory-bridge.md`, hooks in `scripts/codex-hooks/` |\n| agy CLI memory bridge | `docs/agy-memory-bridge.md`, `scripts/agy-sync.ps1` |\n\n## Commands — `.\\scripts\\keystone.ps1 <command>`\n\n`today` · `morning` · `projects` · `resume <Key>` · `context <Key>` · `paths` · `health` · `heal [<Key>]` · `freshness [-Sweep]` · `memory <terms> [-Scope fast|broad]` · `graphify` · `graphsync <Key>` · `status` · `where <Key>` · `start <Key>` · `brief <Key>` · `plan` · `closeout <Key>` · `open <Key>` · `inventory` · `intake` · `promote <path>` · `dashboard` · `cockpit` · `okr-link <Key> <KR-id>` · `agy-sync` · `meeting-sync` · `snapshot`\n\n`health` answers \"do the paths resolve?\" — `freshness` answers \"are the hand-written claims still true?\" The second is the one that decays silently; it runs automatically in the morning cadence.\n\n`.\\scripts\\ritual-check.ps1 [-Notify|-Json]` reports overdue rituals (`/interview-me`, `/weekly-review`). Runs in the morning cadence, and the `KeystoneOS-Rituals` task nudges on weekdays at 17:00 and Fridays at 15:30.\n\n## Scheduled job durability\n\nManaged jobs are declared in `data/jobs.json` and started **only** through `.\\scripts\\run-job.ps1 -Job <id>`, which takes a per-job lock, enforces a timeout, and records the outcome to `outputs/run-ledger.json`. `.\\scripts\\keystone-reconcile.ps1 [-DryRun] [-Json]` re-runs anything with no success recorded for today; the `KeystoneOS-Reconcile` task fires it at logon (+5m) and hourly.\n\nThe rule this encodes: **a scheduled task exiting is not evidence the work happened.** Ask the ledger, or a job's own log via its `successProbe` — never `Get-ScheduledTaskInfo`. On 2026-07-27 the scheduler reported the morning cadence had \"successfully completed\" with a return code that actually meant the process was killed mid-run. See `decisions/log.md` 2026-07-27 and `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-27-scheduled-job-durability-design.md`.\n\nRe-run `.\\scripts\\install-reconcile-task.ps1 -Apply` and `.\\scripts\\harden-scheduled-tasks.ps1 -Apply` after changing task wiring; both are idempotent and dry-run by default.\n\nFront door: when the user says \"work on X\" / \"let's do X\" / \"resume X\", run `.\\scripts\\keystone.ps1 context <X>` FIRST. It resolves the path (self-healing), shows live git, inlines the brief, points at the project's own CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md, and surfaces memory hits + recent decisions — full context in one hop before acting. Paths self-heal on read; `heal` persists a corrected path (auto-commits).\n\nNew project into KeystoneOS: `inventory` → `intake` → `promote <path-or-name> -Status \"Active\"` (writes brief + registry row + projects.json). Map, don't copy — see `decisions/log.md` 2026-06-11.\n\n## Precedence — what wins when two places disagree\n\nRead this before trusting any single file. Two stores disagreeing is the most common way this OS gives a wrong answer.\n\n1. **`AGENTS.md` is the source of truth for routing.** `README.md` and `CLAUDE.md`/`GEMINI.md` defer to it. If they disagree with this table, this table is right and they are stale.\n2. **Generated beats hand-written.** `data/*.json` and anything under `outputs/` beat any `.md` prose describing the same registry. `data/projects.json` beats `projects/registry.md`; `data/memory-sources.json` beats any narrative list of sources.\n3. **Live check beats recorded state.** Any claim about whether a tool is reachable or authenticated (`connections.md`, tool notes) is a hint, not a fact. Run the check command before acting on it.\n4. **Root beats worktree.** `.claude/worktrees/` holds full copies of this repo at older commits. If a search returns two versions of a file, the one at the repo root wins. Never cite a worktree copy as current.\n5. **`decisions/log.md` is the decision record.** Newest entry wins on any conflict with older prose elsewhere.\n\n## Operating rules\n\n- KeystoneOS is a map and control plane, not the source repo for every project.\n- Do not copy large project files into KeystoneOS. Prefer links and local paths to canonical sources.\n- Before multi-step work, find or write a spec (`docs/superpowers/specs/`).\n- Before claiming completion, state and run the verification plan (`verification/default-checklist.md`).\n- Preserve the existing Claude and Codex memory systems; integrate by reading/querying, not overwriting.\n- Use Graphify for comprehension when a repo or corpus is too large to reread directly.\n\n## Harness adapters\n\n`CLAUDE.md` (Claude) and `GEMINI.md` (Gemini) are thin adapters that point here. Keep the three files in sync: shared policy lives in this file only.\n\n## Session routine\n- Start: run `git pull`, then read docs/STATUS.md before doing anything else.\n- End: update docs/STATUS.md (done, next, open questions), commit, and `git push`.\n- Never leave uncommitted work at the end of a session.\n","numLines":90,"startLine":1,"totalLines":90}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c1c4b318-3a48-4b18-96b3-001a7f54e41f","session_id":"51d890bb-1aa4-4397-9981-be25e2430651","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"51d890bb-1aa4-4397-9981-be25e2430651","version":"2.1.281","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"78576fa5-4293-443c-b912-8c00e962dff7","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"nested_memory","path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/CLAUDE.md","content":{"path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/CLAUDE.md","type":"Project","content":"# KeystoneOS Claude Adapter\n\nRead `AGENTS.md` — it is the canonical router and operating policy for this repo. Everything below is Claude-specific only.\n\n- The Claude memory pipeline at `C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\.claude\\claude-memory-compiler` is valuable and must remain in place. KeystoneOS makes that memory visible to other harnesses by reference, never by rewriting it.\n- Claude global working memory lives at `C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\.claude\\global-memory` (USER.md, MEMORY.md, transcripts/). It is enumerated in `data/memory-sources.json` like every other source.\n- Commits to this repo are artifacts, not reviewed code: autonomous commit and push are authorized (decision 2026-06-11, memory `feedback-auto-commit-push`).\n\n## Agent skills\n\n### Issue tracker\n\nIssues live as local markdown files under `.scratch/<feature>/` in this repo. See `docs/agents/issue-tracker.md`.\n\n### Domain docs\n\n**This repo's decision record is `decisions/log.md`** — append-only, one section per decision, current. Read it before proposing architectural changes, and append to it rather than starting a parallel store.\n\n`docs/agents/domain.md` describes the generic `CONTEXT.md` + `docs/adr/` convention used by the engineering skills. Neither exists here and neither is required — that doc says to proceed silently when they're absent. If `/domain-modeling` ever creates them lazily, `decisions/log.md` still wins on any conflict (see the precedence rule in `AGENTS.md`).\n","contentDiffersFromDisk":false},"displayPath":"CLAUDE.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"a0d3d624-dc94-4072-be96-8e04766ffca5","timestamp":"2026-09-25T00:57:41.415Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nContents of /Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/CLAUDE.md:\n\n# KeystoneOS Claude Adapter\n\nRead `AGENTS.md` — it is the canonical router and operating policy for this repo. Everything below is Claude-specific only.\n\n- The Claude memory pipeline at `C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\.claude\\claude-memory-compiler` is valuable and must remain in place. KeystoneOS makes that memory visible to other harnesses by reference, never by rewriting it.\n- Claude global working memory lives at `C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\.claude\\global-memory` (USER.md, MEMORY.md, transcripts/). It is enumerated in `data/memory-sources.json` like every other source.\n- Commits to this repo are artifacts, not reviewed code: autonomous commit and push are authorized (decision 2026-06-11, memory `feedback-auto-commit-push`).\n\n## Agent skills\n\n### Issue tracker\n\nIssues live as local markdown files under `.scratch/<feature>/` in this repo. See `docs/agents/issue-tracker.md`.\n\n### Domain docs\n\n**This repo's decision record is `decisions/log.md`** — append-only, one section per decision, current. Read it before proposing architectural changes, and append to it rather than starting a parallel store.\n\n`docs/agents/domain.md` describes the generic `CONTEXT.md` + `docs/adr/` convention used by the engineering skills. Neither exists here and neither is required — that doc says to proceed silently when they're absent. If `/domain-modeling` ever creates them lazily, `decisions/log.md` still wins on any conflict (see the precedence rule in `AGENTS.md`).\n\n</system-reminder>"}],"session_id":"51d890bb-1aa4-4397-9981-be25e2430651","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"51d890bb-1aa4-4397-9981-be25e2430651","version":"2.1.281","gitBranch":"main"}
