{"parentUuid":"bf28c788-575d-444f-a8b9-5ce3927023f1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfPFS5jJMQEme8vQHJkdy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The sync worked. Everything is clean.\n\n**Sync report**\n- DEV root: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV`\n- Config and skills: all 3 repos pulled and pushed. Skills synced to Codex.\n- Memory moved: `global-memory` got 8 commits from Windows. Newest: `fe55b9c Memory: correct Kitman vs MyLink error`.\n- Two Windows log files (transcripts for 9/23 and 9/24) clashed with the Mac copies. I kept all the text from both sides.\n- Memory mirror: 15 projects paired, 0 files copied, 0 replaced, 0 MEMORY.md merged, 0 twin folders created.\n- 142 repos checked. 9 repos were changed: I committed, pulled, or pushed each one. 1 repo cloned: `RunningTheRoom` (made on Windows today).\n- No `.from-*` files. No repo was created.\n- Dormant repos: all clean.\n\n**Clean: yes.**\n\n**Hook errors from the start of the session**\n- The daily backup failed on 9/23 and 9/24 because `global-memory` was behind GitHub. Today's pull fixed that. The next backup run should pass.\n- The memory compiler has a backlog of 3 logs. To clear it, run `compile.py` by hand.\n\n---\n\n```\nPicking up: KeystoneOS (newest real work: 13:20 today; CFB's later commit was only my sync)\nLast session: 2026-09-24, windows\nWhere things stand: Windows is now the daytime machine, the Mac the evening one. Ritual nudges move to Windows; daily-backup moves to 21:00.\nBlocked on: The Mac half is not done. `com.keystone.rituals` is still loaded, and the Mac backup is still at 09:00. The Mac permission settings blocked this change earlier today.\nNext: Stop `com.keystone.rituals` on the Mac and move the Mac backup to 21:00. Then GPS audit build 2 clean-up (3 old copies to delete by hand).\n```\n\nTell me to continue with this, or name a different project."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,