{"parentUuid":"b61398e0-280f-4b06-b8f6-eacf45a042ea","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfPHQ1JKhT1P9zu2PPBDc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both changes are done on the Mac.\n\n**What I did:**\n- I turned off the Mac rituals job (`com.keystone.rituals`). It stays off after a reboot.\n- I moved the Mac daily backup from 09:00 to 21:00 and reloaded it. `launchctl print` confirms that it now runs at 21:00.\n- I kept a copy of the old backup schedule file: `~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.keystone.dailybackup.plist.bak-2026-09-24`.\n- I added these changes to `KeystoneOS/docs/STATUS.md`. It is committed and pushed. The first push failed because the network dropped. The second push worked.\n\n**What happens next:**\n- Tonight at 21:00 is the first backup at the new time. Plug in the CRASHBOX drive before then if you want the SSD copy too.\n\n**What you do on Windows:**\n- Make sure the `KeystoneOS-Rituals` task is turned on. The rituals nudges now come only from Windows."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":270,"cache_read_input_tokens":114153,"output_tokens":344,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":10},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":270,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":344,"cache_read_input_tokens":114153,"cache_creation_input_tokens":270,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":270},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfPHPzTDdwy4xEWf4C4ga","type":"assistant","uuid":"b8d0b38d-c678-4cb7-bed3-ea296221a261","timestamp":"2026-09-25T01:24:02.272Z","advisorModel":"cla